 typically the dark  square Bishop for white is one of the  least common utilized minor pieces in  the game and so having an opening you  always want to have more than one d4  opening in your repertoire besides the  Queen's Gambit that's very very common  but Bishop here to f4 kind of changes  things up and definitely a very very  solid opening to have four White's  in your opening repertoire  the next opening we're going to be  looking at in their top 10 list is the  cour con previously in our first defense  we looked at how to attack the Queen  pawn opening and this one we're going to  be looking at the King pawn opening  efore it's going to be the same series  of move so its pawn to c6  it usually continues with pawn to d4 and  then black and push forward with pawn to  d5 so as you can tell  same pawn structure as before as the  slob defense but this is more attacking  that first move of pawn here to e4 so  Cara Khan definitely needs to make sure  that you're familiar with this and your  chess openings  the next opening in our top 10 list is  the fried liver attack one of my  favorite attacks because I'm making the  list I get to put some pretty aggressive  openings in here and since I'm a pretty  aggressive player the fried liver attack  is obviously going to make my list if  you're not too familiar pawn to e4 pawn  e5 Knight f3 knight c6 Bishop to c4 and  then after Knight to f6 White's going to  bring his night up here to g5 attacking  with his Bishop and his nights here on  d5 to f7 and then if his opponent  decides to go ahead and try to stop that  with pawn here to d5 we're going to play  pawn capturing after the knight captures  then this nights going to sacrifice here  on f7 so if you like to sacrifice this  is definitely going to be one of your  go-to openings because it's just really  fun who doesn't want their opponent to  bring out their King and then they bring  their Queen involved and they just chase  their opponent's pieces all over the  board so 