ing percentage so you'll  usually see this a lot there's a lot of  ways a lot of different variations of  the Sicilian defense you've got the  knight or if you've got the dragon  you've got your classical you've even  got the accelerated drag and all these  different things I've made videos on all  these but but more than anything you  should definitely be familiar with the  Sicilian defense if you're playing  White's you should be pretty familiar  with how to attack the Sicilian defense  there's different gambits that you have  but this is definitely going to be one  of the most common openings in chess  that everyone should definitely know and  have it in their top 10 chess openings  that they know in chess  and last but not least our number one  chest opening is the Queen's game it's a  pawn here to d4 pawn d5 pawn here to c4  you can watch the video on the Queen's  game but it's not a true gambit y can  actually hold on to the material thie  wants to but this is the most common  opening that you'll see now on chess was  it always this way back in the day there  was more of an aggressive style and you  usually see pawn to e4 more than  anything but in the in the queen pawn  game this this Queens gambit is very  very popular so knowing one how to play  this White's because you may like this  type of opening and as far as blacks  concern finding different openings that  you like to defend against this is very  very popular because you're going to see  this more than pretty much any opening  out there so that is my top 10 list of  the chess openings that you should  definitely learn if you're getting into  chess you've been playing chess for a  while and curious you know if you want  to start playing more what openings you  should know these are the top ten if you  guys want more lists again of different  ways that the top 10 hyper modern or  aggressive or passive or just things for  the top 10 ways to attack the Queen's  Gambit or the Kings game but let me know  I 